{"url": "https://biochemistry.indiana.edu/graduate/how-to-apply/index.html", "final_url": "https://biochemistry.indiana.edu/graduate/how-to-apply/index.html", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-24", "text": "How to Apply: Graduate Program: Interdisciplinary Biochemistry Program: Indiana University Bloomington\nSkip to Content\nSkip to Main Navigation\nSkip to Search\nThe College of Arts & Sciences\nBiochemistry Graduate Program\nHome\nAbout\nDirector of Graduate Studies Message\nFaculty\nStaff\nAbout Bloomington\nGraduate Program\nFunding Opportunities\nStudent Experience\nBIOC Graduate Representative Committee\nCurrent Graduate Students\nHow to Apply\nResearch\nGenome Biochemistry\nSupramolecular Complexes\nPublications\nLabs & Facilities\nSimon Hall Facilities\nIU Facilities\nFaculty Labs\nNews & Events\nProgram News\nBiochemistry Seminar Series\nBMB Research Series\nPh.D. Defenses/Prelims\nSearch\nContact\nStudent Portal\nFunding Opportunities\nStudent Experience\nBIOC Graduate Representative Committee\nCurrent Graduate Students\nHow to Apply\nDomestic Applicants\nInternational Applicants\nHome\nGraduate Program\nHow to Apply\nHow to Apply\nHow to apply\nWe accept students with a broad range of backgrounds in biochemistry, chemistry, or biology. It is helpful if you have had a strong science background that includes biochemistry, organic chemistry, and molecular biology. All applicants must complete and submit the IU Graduate School Application. Please note that there are different requirements for domestic and permanent resident applicants than there are for international applicants.\nWe will review applications received after the priority date; however, we recommend that you submit all application materials by the stated priority date in order to guarantee maximum consideration.\n*We are only accepting applications for the doctoral program at this time.*\nApplication priority date:\nDecember 1, 2026\nApply now\nApplications for Fall 2027 admis